  "modified": "2026-09-28T08:30:21Z",
  "details": "- CVE-2026-39830: drop unsolicited global and channel request responses in the\n  vendored golang.org/x/crypto/ssh mux and channel read paths, so a peer can no\n  longer fill the bounded globalResponses / ch.msg buffers and stall the\n  connection's read loop\n- Rebuild against golang >= 1.25.7-1.el9_6.tuxcare.els16 to pick up the Go\n  standard library fixes for:\n- CVE-2026-33818: enforce a recursion limit in encoding/asn1 Unmarshal to\n  prevent stack exhaustion on deeply nested input\n- CVE-2026-56853: apply ReadHeaderTimeout while sniffing the unencrypted\n  HTTP/2 client preface in net/http\n- CVE-2026-56858: do not close an unescaped '/' early in html/template,\n  preventing attacker-controlled content injection\n- CVE-2026-56859: keep the recursion depth counter across DecodeElement in\n  encoding/xml to prevent stack exhaustion\n- CVE-2026-56860: resolve '..' path segments in net/url with index-based\n  backtracking to remove the quadratic time complexity\n- CVE-2026-56862: only treat post-handshake KeyUpdate messages as\n  state-advancing in crypto/tls, so a client cannot force unbounded key\n  derivation",
